#### GET requests ####

### Get all books
GET http://localhost:4004/browse/Book
Accept: application/json

### Get a single book
GET http://localhost:4004/browse/Book(201)
Accept: application/json

### Get all authors
GET http://localhost:4004/browse/Author
Accept: application/json

### Get all orders
GET http://localhost:4004/browse/Order
Accept: application/json

### Call the Python-backed discount function
GET http://localhost:4004/browse/discount(title='The%20Bestseller')
Accept: application/json

#### POST requests ####

### Create a new author
POST http://localhost:4004/browse/Author
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": 900,
  "name": "Kallol Test Author"
}

### Create a new book (references the author above)
POST http://localhost:4004/browse/Book
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ID": 999,
  "title": "Optimized Book",
  "author_ID": 900,
  "stock": 3,
  "price": 25.00
}

### Ask the Llama AI model through the BTP destination "meta-llama-3-3-70b-instruct"
### Needs `npm run mock:ai` running locally (development profile), or the destination on BTP.
POST http://localhost:4004/ai/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "Recommend two books and explain your choices.",
  "model": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct"
}